A shared life feature: two separate user accounts (seedworks accounts!) can log in, and in settings configure (find other user based on seedworks email) that they are sharing their lives. This is meant mostly for households, people living in one household. In such a case, everyone has their own seedworks account, but their data syncs between eachother. Specifically, they all see the same thing in Banana. They have the same households/pantries, they have the same recipes, and they have the same meal plans. If one user adds another recipe, the other immediately sees it, and can edit it. It essentially should work as if these two people would have one account. For the technical implementation: there should be a "virtual user" created. So when one of these people, in a shared househodld, log in to their banana account, they actually get served the data of another account. And if they leave the household, they get access to their account again, as in if they log out, they wont be redirected to this virtual account anymore.
